{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1382946-mage-fetishes-and-garou-gifts","id":1382946,"title":"Mage Fetishes and Garou Gifts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-21T04:08:38-07:00","id":1382946,"title":"Mage Fetishes and Garou Gifts","content":"Hey, so I have this question for you, people, that I will address later.<br /> <br /> In my game, our Spirit-savvy Mage has created two Fetishes for my Ecstatic and his own Dreamspeaker - the Fetishes were made with a Spirit of War in them, so that they may grant a +10 to initiative score, but our DM flipped his shit, saying that we are not allowed to copy Garou Gifts and make Fetishes out of them. Naturally, we entered a 3 hours argument, but he can't be reasoned with (if you see this, I still hate you, Raven).<br /> <br /> So, my question is: are there any Spirits that we could bind into the Fetish to give the same benefit, but not copy the Spirit of the Fray Garou Gift? They learn this Gift from a Cat Spirit, and they can bind Spirits of War to have it as a Fetish (as per Labrys, Black Fury Fetish). <br /> <br /> I could not find similar Spirits, but I considered using Sands of Time - I doubt it would boost initiative score though. <br /> <br /> What do you people believe? Do you know of such Spirits that could help us end the DM's tyranny? Thanks, and please note them down if you have any idea!<br /> <br /> Have a good day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13197-skeeper0","name":"Skeeper0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T05:27:38-07:00","id":1382961,"title":"","content":"For clarity in giving you good advice:<br /> <br /> Is your ST allowing your mages to craft Fetishes have follow Werewolf Fetish rules, or are Fetishes made by mages crafted only using the Wonder crafting rules presented in Mage (in whichever edition you're using)? Because that's going to impact a lot.<br /> <br /> That said... unless you're playing in a mixed game with Garou (either as PCs or NPCs using full Garou rules) you're never going to need Spirit of the Fray. An improvement of +3 or +4 is enough beat non-supernaturals with ease, and is on par with many supernatural powers that likely cost more for much shorter duration than you can get from a Wonder or Mage magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T05:51:56-07:00","id":1382963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1382946-mage-fetishes-and-garou-gifts?p=1382961#post1382961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For clarity in giving you good advice:<br /> <br /> Is your ST allowing your mages to craft Fetishes have follow Werewolf Fetish rules, or are Fetishes made by mages crafted only using the Wonder crafting rules presented in Mage (in whichever edition you're using)? Because that's going to impact a lot.<br /> <br /> That said... unless you're playing in a mixed game with Garou (either as PCs or NPCs using full Garou rules) you're never going to need Spirit of the Fray. An improvement of +3 or +4 is enough beat non-supernaturals with ease, and is on par with many supernatural powers that likely cost more for much shorter duration than you can get from a Wonder or Mage magic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> We follow the Mage Wonder crafting rules presented in MtA20th (we play in the same chronicle, 20th anniv.) and yes, it's a cross-splat between Mages, Vampires, Werewolves, Demons, and Changelings.<br /> <br /> Usually, people run around with a base of at least 18 initiative with a 1 in the roll (5 dexterity, 5 celerity, 5 wits, Vitae buffs/ Spirit of the Fray which is given like it's warm bread) - myself, as a Master of Time (Time 5 and other Spheres at 4), I could get killed on the street by a 12th generation Vampire with a grudge or a Fostern that simply does not like me being in the forest at the borders of their bawn, and that is frequent enough.<br /> <br /> The ST allowed us to craft Fetishes, excluding the Fetishes that employ Garou Gifts, so I am looking for a way to get a higher initiative without copying the Spirit of the Fray Gift, preferably using a Spirit bound in a Fetish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13197-skeeper0","name":"Skeeper0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T09:25:21-07:00","id":1382984,"title":"","content":"Hmm\u2026 I don't know the specifics of the situation; but if it's legal under the M20 Fetish rules, it shouldn't matter whether or not there's a Garou Gift that works similarly. That is, you shouldn't be named from doing something that would otherwise be permissible solely because the Garou can do it. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, if the only reason why it works is because you're borrowing game mechanics from Werewolf (e.g., the M20 Fetish rules don't permit it, but there's a Garou Gift that permits it), then your Storyteller has a point. <br /> <br /> In a nutshell, the Werewolf rules ought to have nothing to do with what a Spirit mage can do either way: it should neither restrict them nor empower them further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T12:43:07-07:00","id":1383017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1382946-mage-fetishes-and-garou-gifts?p=1382984#post1382984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the other hand, if the only reason why it works is because you're borrowing game mechanics from Werewolf (e.g., the M20 Fetish rules don't permit it, but there's a Garou Gift that permits it), then your Storyteller has a point.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The reason he does not want us to have the Spirit of the Fray Gift made as a Fetish is that he believes that will ruin the Werewolf immersion - the fact that we can get such Fetishes that employ their Gifts, thus banned all Fetishes that use Gifts as effects. He can't be reasoned with, which is why I came here to ask for help in finding a Spirit or any sort, or Effect, that might increase one's Initiative with 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13197,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13197-skeeper0","user":"Skeeper0","date":". 04-21-2020, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13197-skeeper0","name":"Skeeper0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T13:00:13-07:00","id":1383021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skeeper0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1382946-mage-fetishes-and-garou-gifts#post1382946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, so I have this question for you, people, that I will address later.<br /> <br /> In my game, our Spirit-savvy Mage has created two Fetishes for my Ecstatic and his own Dreamspeaker - the Fetishes were made with a Spirit of War in them, so that they may grant a +10 to initiative score, but our DM flipped his shit, saying that we are not allowed to copy Garou Gifts and make Fetishes out of them. Naturally, we entered a 3 hours argument, but he can't be reasoned with (if you see this, I still hate you, Raven).<br /> <br /> So, my question is: are there any Spirits that we could bind into the Fetish to give the same benefit, but not copy the Spirit of the Fray Garou Gift? They learn this Gift from a Cat Spirit, and they can bind Spirits of War to have it as a Fetish (as per Labrys, Black Fury Fetish).<br /> <br /> I could not find similar Spirits, but I considered using Sands of Time - I doubt it would boost initiative score though.<br /> <br /> What do you people believe? Do you know of such Spirits that could help us end the DM's tyranny? Thanks, and please note them down if you have any idea!<br /> <br /> Have a good day.</div> </div> </div> </div>In general I would state my case to the Storyteller but if they don't think its appropriate for their game I would give them the benefit of the doubt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T13:19:47-07:00","id":1383023,"title":"","content":"More importantly, the Storyteller's word on this is final. If he says no and can't be reasoned with, no one here is going to be able to help you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T13:45:33-07:00","id":1383030,"title":"","content":"I've always found very interesting the interplay between what Spirits can do themselves (i.e, their Charms), the Gifts they can teach, and what Spirits do when put into Fetishes--I've never seen Gift that perfectly mimicked the mechanical operation of a Spirit Charm (or vice versa), and I 've never seen a Fetish that did either, and I haven't seen textual examples of a Spirit itself using a Gift that it teaches to Garou (many of which wouldn't make sense for a spirit to do). There's just no hard and fast rule which allow you to sysmetically suss out what exactly you can achieve when putting any given type of spirit into Fetish, <i>other than</i> simply looking at Fetishes already codified in the books and saying &quot;well, you can definitely make one <i>those</i>.&quot; Mind you, this goes for Werewolves and Mages alike; I've played Werewolf games where I wanted to make X fetish or talen, and the ST just sorta had to look at it and (a) evaluate whether it made some thematic sense that a spirit of whatever type would allow you do <i>whatever</i> power, and (b) the power level had to feel right in light of the power level of other fetishes, gifts, etc.<br /> <br /> It's a super loose analysis. Personally, I think it'd be putting you between a rock and a hard place to completely shut you out of being able to reference extant Spirit powers, gifts, etc., in order to make a Fetish; like I said above, they're the only things you really have to go by.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T16:11:51-07:00","id":1383050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1382946-mage-fetishes-and-garou-gifts?p=1383030#post1383030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a super loose analysis. Personally, I think it'd be putting you between a rock and a hard place to completely shut you out of being able to reference extant Spirit powers, gifts, etc., in order to make a Fetish; like I said above, they're the only things you really have to go by.</div> </div> </div> </div> This. In particular, fetishes have always been something of a Werewolf crossover thing in Mage, just as spirits themselves have been. Heck, just look at what the game stats for spirits are: Willpower, Rage, Gnosis, Essence, etc. If I were the Storyteller, I wouldn't put any restrictions on what a Mage-made Fetish can do that isn't on what a Garou-made Fetish can do, or vice versa. Where they'd be different would be on how you go about making them: I'd look closely at each gameline's system for making Fetishes, and I'd tweak one or both as needed to give the Garou an easier time making them. <br /> <br /> But while I agree that it sounds like your Storyteller is being unreasonable, that doesn't change the fact that he still has final say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T18:19:12-07:00","id":1383060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skeeper0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1382946-mage-fetishes-and-garou-gifts?p=1382963#post1382963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I could get killed on the street by a 12th generation Vampire with a grudge or a Fostern that simply does not like me being in the forest at the borders of their bawn, and that is frequent enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're over stressing initiative here. They just get to go first, they still need to defeat your defenses and avoid your attacks in response.<br /> <br /> First off, Sphere magic can boost Initiative indirectly by boosting Dexterity and Wits (Life 3/Mind 1). So increasing init isn't something foreign to mages and you can use that magic in combination with a Fetish.<br /> <br /> Second, M20's expanded Wonder crafting in Book of Secrets says to use the guideline of &quot;the Fetish's Gnosis rating = bonus.&quot; So, don't want to copy Spirit of the Fray for +10, because that means the difficulty to activate it is 10, but you could make a Gnosis 6 or 7 Fetish for +6 or 7 to your init. If you need an idea for a spirit, you can always use hummingbird... as a Garou Totem Hummingbird gives Spirit of the Fray as a Gift to its followers (and boosts Dexterity!), so it's at least a good thematic choice for a initiative boosting Fetish. So +6 from your hummingbird Fetish and +4 or +6 from boosting your Attributes? There, you're competitive with everyone else.<br /> <br /> Third, a good use of a spirit of war for a Fetish could be something like letting you use Melee Parries with the associated Rebound Attacks, when using Desperate Defense. Let the Garou or Vampire jump you, declare Desperate Defense and activating your awesome parry dagger Fetish, which probably does Aggravated damage too. Have a running Magic Enhancing Abilities effect going to reduce your Melee difficulties by 3 to really mess up anyone that things going first means they're shred you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T22:44:20-07:00","id":1383096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1382946-mage-fetishes-and-garou-gifts?p=1383060#post1383060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, Sphere magic can boost Initiative indirectly by boosting Dexterity and Wits (Life 3/Mind 1). So increasing init isn't something foreign to mages and you can use that magic in combination with a Fetish.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is even a Corr 1 / Time 1 rote in the older ItX book that allows raising initiative at a per-success rate.<br /> <br /> Craft that stuff into a charm with some duration and a pile of successes, and you're golden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T04:49:26-07:00","id":1383124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1382946-mage-fetishes-and-garou-gifts?p=1383060#post1383060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Second, M20's expanded Wonder crafting in Book of Secrets says to use the guideline of &quot;the Fetish's Gnosis rating = bonus.&quot; So, don't want to copy Spirit of the Fray for +10, because that means the difficulty to activate it is 10, but you could make a Gnosis 6 or 7 Fetish for +6 or 7 to your init. If you need an idea for a spirit, you can always use hummingbird... as a Garou Totem Hummingbird gives Spirit of the Fray as a Gift to its followers (and boosts Dexterity!), so it's at least a good thematic choice for a initiative boosting Fetish. So +6 from your hummingbird Fetish and +4 or +6 from boosting your Attributes? There, you're competitive with everyone else.<br /> <br /> Third, a good use of a spirit of war for a Fetish could be something like letting you use Melee Parries with the associated Rebound Attacks, when using Desperate Defense. Let the Garou or Vampire jump you, declare Desperate Defense and activating your awesome parry dagger Fetish, which probably does Aggravated damage too. Have a running Magic Enhancing Abilities effect going to reduce your Melee difficulties by 3 to really mess up anyone that things going first means they're shred you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm..I did not know such a Totem existed - could you redirect me its way, please? I can't find it in MtA nor WtA20th. <br /> <br /> Also, a question about the Rebound Attack move - say, that my attacker scored 5 successes on their brawl attack, and I scored 8 to parry it using my Awakened Great Sword which does 7/Agg by itself. Does that mean that I roll 10 dice of damage on the attacker, or do I have to roll an attack as if I would normally be attacking? MtA has a way of confusing me at times.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13197-skeeper0","name":"Skeeper0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T04:50:12-07:00","id":1383125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1382946-mage-fetishes-and-garou-gifts?p=1383096#post1383096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is even a Corr 1 / Time 1 rote in the older ItX book that allows raising initiative at a per-success rate.<br /> <br /> Craft that stuff into a charm with some duration and a pile of successes, and you're golden.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We already did that, but it's hard to compete against many Vampires that have Thaumaturgy: Focused Mind, when they should not and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13197-skeeper0","name":"Skeeper0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T12:08:20-07:00","id":1383186,"title":"","content":"Hummingbird hasn't been updated from W20, it's from Uktena Revised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}